codex
The module is locally complete and reproducible: all nine local gate groups pass, including exact uniqueness, 200,000 structure-aware guesses, four failing attacks, doubled-size construction, and 60 composed relabelling checks. The README and required reports are written. The only unfinished requirement is the external oracle evidence, which cannot proceed until the OpenRouter key’s total limit is raised or reset.
The generator, local verification, reports, and README are complete. The mandatory bare/G9 oracle runs were invoked through the prescribed harness but all calls returned HTTP 403 key-limit errors, leaving the external hardness claim genuinely blocked.
  ✓ Read the full paper and identify the native problem, construction theorem, verification route, and algorithmic cost
  ✓ Decide Track A/B or rejection and design a construction-backed family in the paper’s native objects
  ✓ Implement the generator module and comprehensive selftest gates
  ✓ Run selftests, adversarial measurements, canonical invariance checks, and fix issues
  • Run the required oracle hardening and G9 arms if credentials permit
  ✓ Write README and final machine-readable reports
