codex
The first revised version passed the required eight attack seeds, but a broader 200-seed audit showed the naïve “closest selected values” heuristic still won 19 times. I’m tightening the inverse construction so two harmless singleton components always supply a closer cross-component decoy, while every selected point still has exactly the same block degree. This makes the generic failures construction-backed instead of seed luck.
apply patch
