 """Verified problem generator for arXiv:2601.04295.
 
-The paper gives a 30-block family on 60 points and proves that every six
-selected points have a pair in one of its blocks.  This module composes exact
-copies of that construction and adds harmless six-block decoys containing at
-most one selected point.  The planted pair and block are carried through the
-composition; generation never searches for a witness.
+The paper's 30 blocks are five disjoint 12-point components.  Each component
+is split into four triples and contains all six unions of two triples.  This
+module composes those exact native components, inverse-plants one selected
+pair in distinct triples, and fills every other occupied component with at
+most one selected point.  Generation therefore carries the unique witness;
+it never searches for one.
 """
 
