codex
A broader seed audit exposed a generator-totality bug in the rejected prototype: a defensive decoy constraint could exhaust its local choices on some seeds. I fixed it by constructing the harmless labels `1,2` algebraically instead of searching for them, then verified 1,000 demo/easy seeds and 300 medium/hard seeds with no construction, certificate, compact-solver, or attack failures. Because that changes the generated instances, I’m rerunning the rejection oracle evidence once more so the transcript matches the preserved module exactly.
exec
