codex
Rejected: the paper cannot support an acceptable hard family.

- Track A fails because Sections 2–3 provide an explicit linear-time construction and witness algorithm, with no hard regime.
- The strongest Track B prototype passed all local gates, but the mandatory oracle loop solved 9/9 instances—3/3 at every preset—yielding `too_easy`.
- Further padding would only increase prompt length while leaving the discovered compact route unchanged.

Deliverables:

- [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2601.04295/REJECTED.md)
- [Preserved prototype](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2601.04295/rejected_gen_2601_04295.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2601.04295/selftest_report.json)
- [Oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2601.04295/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2601.04295/README.md)

The decision is based on the complete [arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.04295), not only its abstract.
