-# arXiv 2601.04295 — verified pair-in-a-block witnesses
-
-**Status:** the generator and every local gate pass. The mandatory oracle claim is
-**not established**: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded` for every
-bare, structural-hint, and placebo call. The script-owned error transcripts are
-retained and must be replaced by a successful run after quota is restored.
-
-| Profile field | Value |
-|---|---|
-| Track | **B** — no-tool compression; ordinary software solves every instance |
-| Native domain | combinatorics |
-| Object regime | finite discrete |
-| Computational core | other (exact block-incidence witness search) |
-| Certificate form | integer tuple, encoded as a selected pair plus a six-element block |
-| Intended intuition | decomposition into 12-point/four-triple components |
-| Domain essentiality | native |
-| Reduction | none |
-
-## Problem and provenance
-
-[Gomes, “An explicit family of 30 blocks meeting every 6-set of [60] in at
-least two points”](https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.04295) partitions ten six-point
-base blocks into five pairs. Section 2 splits each base block into two triples
-and adds the four cross-base triple unions. Equivalently, each paired couple is
-a 12-point component split into four triples, and its two base blocks plus four
-recombinations are exactly all six unions of two triples. Theorem 1 proves that
-any six selected points contain a pair in a listed block.
-
-An instance composes those exact 12-point components and shuffles all blocks.
-Exactly one component gets two selected points in distinct triples; every other
-component gets at most one. The answer is the two selected points and their
-unique pair-of-triples block. Checking types, ordering, selected membership,
-listed-block membership, and containment is exact and cheap. Generation samples
-the answer-bearing component first and carries its union block; it never solves
-the emitted instance. Every distractor block comes from the same Section 2
-component construction as the witness block.
-
-## Why Track B, not Track A
-
-The paper contains no hardness theorem or hard parameter regime. Its Section 3
-proof is itself a short witness algorithm on the fixed 60-point example, so a
-Track A claim would be false. This module instead grows a certificate-safe
-haystack by disjoint composition.
-
-The disclosed reference algorithm scans the shuffled blocks and tests their six
-entries against the selected set. It is exact, succeeds 8/8 as expected, and is
-`O(6m)` for `m` blocks. At the shipping preset it averaged **3,688 membership
-tests** and **0.0002–0.0011 seconds** across repeated runs. After recognizing Section 2's component
-decomposition, a no-tool solver scans the sorted selected values for the one
-repeated 12-point quotient and writes the union of the two corresponding
-triples. The measured maximum was 198 exact operations; the conservative bound
-is **238**. That mechanical-versus-compact gap is the Track B claim.
-
-The easy regime that had to be avoided is the paper's single five-component
-instance: its complete block scan is only 180 memberships, and its proof route
-is shorter still. Padding adds only exact paper components, so it lengthens the
-scan without lengthening the eight-atom certificate or the compact route.
-
-## Worked demo (`n=1`, seed `0`)
-
-This is the complete rendered demo and is hand-solvable.
-
-```text
-PAIR-IN-A-BLOCK WITNESS
-
-The ground set is the integers 1 through 60, inclusive.
-A block is an unordered set of exactly six distinct ground-set integers.
-The selected set S is:
-12 13 33 42 45 53
-
-The block family has 30 blocks. Block numbering below is only for readability:
-0: 1 2 3 4 5 6
-1: 37 38 39 43 44 45
-2: 25 26 27 34 35 36
-3: 40 41 42 43 44 45
-4: 40 41 42 46 47 48
-5: 31 32 33 34 35 36
-6: 1 2 3 10 11 12
-7: 55 56 57 58 59 60
-8: 13 14 15 19 20 21
-9: 7 8 9 10 11 12
-10: 16 17 18 22 23 24
-11: 25 26 27 31 32 33
-12: 49 50 51 52 53 54
-13: 1 2 3 7 8 9
-14: 52 53 54 58 59 60
-15: 43 44 45 46 47 48
-16: 13 14 15 22 23 24
-17: 4 5 6 7 8 9
-18: 37 38 39 46 47 48
-19: 52 53 54 55 56 57
-20: 4 5 6 10 11 12
-21: 28 29 30 34 35 36
-22: 13 14 15 16 17 18
-23: 37 38 39 40 41 42
-24: 19 20 21 22 23 24
-25: 28 29 30 31 32 33
-26: 16 17 18 19 20 21
-27: 49 50 51 58 59 60
-28: 49 50 51 55 56 57
-29: 25 26 27 28 29 30
-
-Find two distinct elements x<y of S and one listed block containing both x and y.
-Return the block itself, not its displayed line number. Write both arrays in strictly increasing order.
-Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags as one JSON object.
-This numeric example illustrates syntax only; it is not the answer to this instance:
-<answer>{"pair":[3,17],"block":[1,2,3,17,18,19]}</answer>
-Replace all eight numbers with your witness. Output nothing else inside the tags.
-```
-
-The answer is
-`{"pair":[42,45],"block":[40,41,42,43,44,45]}` and `verify` returns
-`(True, "ok")`. Dropping `45` from the pair returns
-`(False, "pair must contain exactly two integers")`.
-
-## Difficulty ladder
-
-The number of selected singleton components varies with the seed from 64 to
-111 on non-demo presets; the table therefore gives candidate-space ranges.
-
-| Preset | Paper copies `n` | Padding components | Blocks | Selected points | Candidate space |
-|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
-| demo | 1 | 0 | 30 | 6 | 450 |
-| easy (**ships provisionally**) | 32 | 64 | 1,344 | 66–113 | 2,882,880–8,504,832 |
-| medium | 40 | 160 | 2,160 | 66–113 | 4,633,200–13,668,480 |
-| hard | 50 | 300 | 3,300 | 66–113 | 7,078,500–20,882,400 |
-
-No rung failed a local gate. `SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY` remains provisional at
-`easy`; the script must own any escalation after a scoreable oracle run.
-
-## Gate results
-
-| Gate | Result | Measurement |
-|---|---|---|
-| G1 | pass | 12/12 planted witnesses; exactly one valid answer in every tested instance |
-| G2 | pass | 5/5 corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
-| G3 | pass | tagged JSON round-tripped through prose and a Markdown fence |
-| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 hits; exact shipping density `1/5,263,104 = 1.9000e-7` |
-| G5 | pass | exact shipping count 1; strongest failing attack used 2,048 restart trials total |
-| G6 | pass | four attacks at 0/8; direct scan and compact reference each solve 8/8 |
-| G7 | pass | doubling `n` gives 2,304 blocks and 11,635,200 candidates for the tested seed |
-| G8 | pass | 60/60 relabelling invariance and carried-witness checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
-| G9(c) | pass | 60 characters, about 15 tokens, 8 atoms, 238 intended operations |
-
-The four failing attacks are selected-point degree outliers, the closest-value
-greedy pair, 256 structure-aware random restarts, and the paper's first-case
-same-base-block ansatz. Every selected point has degree three. The harmless
-cross-component pair `12,13` defeats the first two tie/greedy choices, points in
-the witness component use opposite base blocks, and the unique witness defeats
-uniform restarts. A separate 200-seed audit gave 0 successes for the three
-deterministic attacks.
-
-## Oracle loop and G9 arms
+# arXiv 2601.04295 — rejected after Track B hardening
 
-These are script-authored calls, but none is scoreable because the credential
-was quota-blocked. The repository's current harness advertised a two-model pool
-(`openai/gpt-5.6-terra`, `google/gemini-3.8-flash`) during this run.
-
-| Arm | Preset | Seeds attempted | Valid solved/attempts | Outcome |
-|---|---|---|---:|---|
-| bare | easy | 103137434, 111365809, 534775670, 1829126921 | 0/0 | 4 HTTP 403 key-limit errors; no verdict |
-| structural | easy | 586082484, 2031957973, 131842738, 130828869 | 0/0 | 4 HTTP 403 key-limit errors; no verdict |
-| placebo | easy | 1883865491, 1615184326, 138649172, 997305585 | 0/0 | 4 HTTP 403 key-limit errors; no verdict |
-
-Hinted minus placebo is undefined because both denominators are zero. There is
-therefore no evidential conclusion about the decomposition hint yet. The hint
-names only the 12-point/four-triple invariant and does not prescribe the next
-step.
+This directory contains a preserved, locally verified prototype for Gomes,
+[“An explicit family of 30 blocks meeting every 6-set of [60] in at least two
+points”](https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.04295), but it is **not a shippable problem
+family**. Read [REJECTED.md](REJECTED.md) for the full quantitative decision.
 
-## Use
+The paper's Section 2 object is native and retained: each 12-point component is
+split into four triples and carries all six unions of two triples. The prototype
+composes these components, inverse-plants a unique pair-and-block witness, and
+carries it through an exact modular relabeling. Every local correctness,
+guess-resistance, adversary, scaling, canonicalization, and output-cap gate
+passes.
 
-```python
-import gen_2601_04295 as g
+The family nevertheless fails H. Track A is unavailable because Theorem 1's
+proof is itself a short witness algorithm and the paper proves no hard regime.
+For Track B, the reference incidence scan is `O(6m)` and used a measured mean of
+5,849 tests at `easy` and 17,295 at `hard`; the modular/decomposition shortcut
+uses at most 295 exact operations. The mandatory no-tool pool found that
+shortcut and solved 9/9 calls—3/3 at each of `easy`, `medium`, and `hard`.
+`.meta.json` records the resulting `too_easy` verdict.
 
-params = g.DIFFICULTY[g.SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY]
-inst = g.make_instance(seed=123, **params)
-question = g.render(inst)
-ok, reason = g.verify(inst, inst["answer"])
-assert (ok, reason) == (True, "ok")
-```
+The `prior_g9_*_quota_blocked` files are retained only as an audit of an older
+prototype whose G9 calls received HTTP 403. No final G9 arms were run: the bare
+STEP 4 loop had already rejected the family, so hinted/placebo diagnostics could
+not rescue it and would only spend oracle calls.
 
-After a successful hardening rerun, emit from the repository root with:
+The attempted module is preserved as `rejected_gen_2601_04295.py`, as required
+for audit and possible future analysis. It may be run directly to reproduce the
+local self-test, but it must not be emitted as a dataset family:
 
 ```bash
-bash scripts/emit.sh 2601.04295 20
+python3 rejected_gen_2601_04295.py
 ```
-
-## Caveats
-
-This family is easy with ordinary code; that is the disclosed Track B reference
-algorithm. It may also be easy without tools for a model that notices the
-consecutive 12-point quotient and reliably scans up to 113 selected values. The
-numeric labels deliberately preserve that compact structure; an arbitrary
-ground-set relabelling preserves the mathematical problem and canonical key but
-erases the human shortcut.
-
-The G4 probability is only for the declared prior—uniform selected pairs times
-uniform listed blocks. It does not model a theorem-aware solver, and a large
-candidate space alone is not evidence of hardness. At the shipping preset there
-are only 48 isomorphism types generated by the varying singleton count; the
-emitter can resample duplicates, while larger `n` supplies an unbounded family.
-No SAT, ILP, or spectral method is relevant to this direct witness objective;
-the exact incidence scan is the stronger applicable standard method. Most
-importantly, no vendor-hardness claim should be trusted until the 403 blocker is
-removed and all three arms are rerun successfully.
